Packaging layout and rebase workflow
====================================

This is a fork of ubuntu/gnome-shell-extension-appindicator. The branch
layout is deliberately kept as simple as possible so that following
upstream is a plain rebase:

  master      tracks upstream, never modified by us
  sinambung   master + a single commit adding debian/

The packaging adds files under debian/ and changes nothing else. No
upstream-owned file is patched -- not meson.build, not metadata.json, not
the root .gitignore. Build artifacts are kept inside debian/build (see
--builddirectory in debian/rules) and are covered by debian/.gitignore,
so upstream's own .gitignore needs no edits either.

The consequence is that `git rebase upstream/master` should never
conflict. If it ever does, that is a signal we started patching upstream
files and should reconsider.

Remotes
-------

  origin     git@github.com:BlankOn/appindicator-gnome-shell-extension.git
  upstream   https://github.com/ubuntu/gnome-shell-extension-appindicator.git

Following a new upstream release
--------------------------------

  git fetch --tags upstream
  git checkout master && git merge --ff-only upstream/master && git push origin master
  git checkout sinambung && git rebase upstream/master

Then record the new version. The package version is taken solely from
debian/changelog -- upstream's meson.build version field is left alone,
even when it lags behind the git tag -- so a release is:

  dch -v <upstream-version>-1
  git commit -am "Bump to <upstream-version>-1."
  git push --force-with-lease origin sinambung

Note that debian/changelog must be bumped for any change to reach users:
appindicator-update-user.sh keys the per-user copy in ~/.local/share on
the dpkg version recorded in .installed-version, so without a new version
the user copy is never refreshed.

Building
--------

  dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b
  debian/rules clean      # leaves the tree pristine for rebasing
